  "instructions": [
    "Heat 1 tablespoon of oil in a small pan over medium heat.",
    "Add fenugreek seeds, cumin seeds, and red chili flakes; toast until fragrant, about 30 seconds. Remove and set aside.",
    "In a large pot, heat the remaining 1 tablespoon of oil over medium heat. Add diced onion, carrot, and bell pepper; saut\u00e9 until softened, about 5 minutes.",
    "Stir in the ginger and garlic paste and cook for 1 minute until aromatic.",
    "Add tomato puree, cumin, coriander, smoked paprika, cinnamon, turmeric, salt, and black pepper; cook, stirring, for 2 minutes.",
    "Pour in the chickpeas and vegetable broth, then fold in almond butter. Bring to a gentle simmer.",
    "Return the toasted tempering mixture to the pot, stir, and let the stew simmer uncovered for 15\u201320 minutes, allowing flavors to meld and the stew to thicken.",
    "Taste and adjust seasoning if needed. Let the stew cool if storing for meal\u2011prep.",
    "Reheat portions in the microwave or on the stovetop and garnish with chopped parsley before serving."
  ],
